What tam-pane is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-22, with W28


STATE

  Version 0.2.3 on branch dev, accepted by Fred on 2026-11-22 after his
  nested sandbox/demo-0.2.3 check (W28). Phase P3: 0.2.3 adds a same-UID
  Unix domain IPC socket ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tam-pane/<socket>.sock,
  exported as TAM_PANE_SOCKET) with a line-based request/reply and
  event-stream format built with libtam's tam_str_* helpers (no cJSON),
  a `tam-pane msg` client subcommand, and arch/ipc.md. Commands: version,
  monitors, windows, focused, tags, cursor, binds, reload, dispatch,
  subscribe. While locked, queries, subscribe, and reload stay allowed
  and dispatch returns ERR session is locked. R1 finding 17's SIGHUP
  point is resolved: SIGHUP now triggers clean shutdown like
  SIGTERM/SIGINT, and live reloads use `tam-pane msg reload` or
  tp.dsp.reload().
